DERIVED SOURCE CODE
===================

Unlike the tools bundled with the desktop application (below), the following is not run
at arm's length: it is source code in this program, derived from another project's:

  cyberdrop-dl    https://github.com/jbsparrow/CyberDropDownloader
                  GNU General Public License v3.0

                  The file-host site extractors in
                  src/sift/slices/download/sources/sites/ (their endpoints, page
                  selectors, signing flows, and the JPG5/Bunkr crypto) were followed
                  from cyberdrop-dl's crawlers to read sites yt-dlp and gallery-dl do
                  not handle. Those files carry the same attribution in their headers.

                  Sift is licensed AGPL-3.0, which is compatible with GPL-3.0: AGPLv3
                  section 13 and GPLv3 section 13 each permit linking with the other,
                  so this derived code may ship in an AGPL-3.0 work.

                  cyberdrop-dl's LICENSE file names no copyright holder; the
                  project's pyproject.toml names its author as Jacob B.


