BUNDLED WITH THE WINDOWS DESKTOP APPLICATION
===========================================

  The desktop application installs nothing from a package manager: it carries its
  own copies of the external tools it runs. It runs each as a separate process and
  does not link against them or import them as libraries, so they remain
  independent works under their own licenses. Each is redistributed unmodified.
  They are pinned by SHA-256 in scripts/vendor_manifest.json and fetched by
  scripts/fetch_vendor.py, which verifies the hash before unpacking and refuses to
  substitute a different build.

  FFmpeg / FFprobe        vendor/bin/ffmpeg.exe, vendor/bin/ffprobe.exe, and the
                          eight libraries they share: avcodec-61.dll, avdevice-61.dll,
                          avfilter-10.dll, avformat-61.dll, avutil-59.dll,
                          postproc-58.dll, swresample-5.dll, swscale-8.dll.
                          n7.1.5, the win64-gpl-SHARED build. Shared rather than
                          static because the static build compiles every codec into
                          both executables: 278 MB against 160 MB for exactly the same
                          capability, on every install and every update download.
                          Built with --enable-gpl and --enable-version3, so these are
                          GPL-3.0-or-later. The full licence text ships beside them as
                          vendor/bin/ffmpeg-LICENSE.txt.
                          The build is FFmpeg at commit 9a4bb2c579 on the release/7.1
                          branch (n7.1.5-16-g9a4bb2c579, as `ffmpeg -version` reports),
                          built by BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds. Its complete source ships as
                          vendor/bin/sources/ffmpeg-n7.1.5-16-g9a4bb2c579.tar.gz.
                          Compiled into the libraries with it, and shipped as source
                          beside it:
                            x264 at 0480cb05fa18 (GPL-2.0-or-later)
                              vendor/bin/sources/x264-0480cb05fa18.tar.gz
                            x265 4.2+37 at b81f650e21e8 (GPL-2.0-or-later)
                              vendor/bin/sources/x265-4.2-37-b81f650e21e8.tar.gz
                          The scripts that built it ship as
                          vendor/bin/sources/FFmpeg-Builds-590a6612d7d9.tar.gz; they
                          name, by exact commit, every other library compiled into
                          these files (scripts.d/, SCRIPT_COMMIT), with the address
                          each one's source is published at. Among them is
                          Chromaprint (scripts.d/50-chromaprint.sh), which Sift reads
                          a file's audio fingerprint with.

  libwebp tools           vendor/bin/webpinfo.exe, vendor/bin/anim_dump.exe
